Z||000020||Monkeyman||06-21-2001||06:11 PM||||Huck--I'm not worried about it getting kicked, but I have a big elbow.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  No sense taking any chances.  The "hockey mask" idea is a good one.  The only detail I can't figure out is how to mount it on the sub without looking stupid.  If I just lay it on top of the sub, I'll have the trim ring showing as well as the edge of the Lexan/Plexi.  Any suggestions??<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000021||Seanh||06-22-2001||01:37 PM||||Not sure what to say on that one. I always cut a little stair step into the box, and mount the top of the sub flush or under the surface of the box, then the grill sits right on the box and looks good. Look at AudioBahn sub grilles, they have some chrome ones that I think look astounding. <P>BTW, excellent choice on the Vega. Its not one that came to mind with me, probally because I don't work with them that often. I would not be concerned with having any trouble with their paper cones. With brands like Cerwin, their paper cones are excellent quality, and will probally last a very long time. They do crack when they are overpowered. I have an AudioBahn system in one of my other cars, and I'm overpower each of 2 12" subs by 150w RMS, and they cracked. I really beat them though. I'm going with carbon fiber cones for replacement.||||reg||1
